{"name":"Aquarelle Lilac","hex":"#edc8ff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aquarelle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A watercolour (painting)","A printed picture coloured by the application of watercolour through stencils, using a different stencil for each colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquarelle"},{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Watercolor painting","blocks":[{"text":"Watercolor or watercolour, also aquarelle, is a painting method in which the paints are made of pigments suspended in a water-based solution. Watercolor refers to both the medium and the resulting artwork."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg/330px-Dolceacqua43_-_Artista_locale_mentre_dipinge_un_acquarello.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watercolor_painting","wikidata":"Q50030"},{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"L